   plot="The sermons are single-argument meditations on the creed, the sacraments, sin, conscience and the unseen world, delivered to an academic congregation and designed to awaken a sense of the reality of God; the most famous, 'The Second Spring' (1852), belongs to the later Catholic collection.",
   context="The 1830s at Oxford, the Noetics and the Oriel common room, the Evangelical revival and the High Church reaction that became the Oxford Movement.",
