   attrib="A free adaptation rather than a literal translation: FitzGerald selected, rearranged and partly invented quatrains from the Persian and constructed a continuous poem. The first edition (1859) has 75 quatrains; the fourth (1879) has 101 and is the text usually reprinted.",
